# Stage lighting
@scenario tutorial_lesson_24
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Take a look at my face before I change the stage lights. Do those shadows still fall in the same place?
[stage dusk]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move ginger guide normal exprdur=0]
[move ginger rightmark ease_in_out_cubic 640]
[wait 160]
[move ginger rightmark normal exprdur=0]
[wait 160]
[move ginger rightmark normal exprdur=0]
[wait 160]
[move ginger rightmark normal exprdur=0]
[wait 160]
[move ginger rightmark thoughtful exprdur=90]
[endif]
ginger: The dusk preset is active. Notice the cooler stage and warm key light.
[stage clear]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move ginger rightmark normal exprdur=0]
[move ginger guide ease_out_cubic 510]
[wait 120]
[move ginger guide normal exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move ginger guide normal exprdur=0]
[wait 120]
[move ginger guide normal exprdur=0]
[wait 150]
[move ginger guide normal exprdur=90]
[endif]
ginger: Open dusk.stagepreset in Lighting Studio, adjust exposure, and compare the result in Puppeteer.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: How do you restore the original lighting in VNS?
> Hide Ginger. -> retry
> Use the stage clear command. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Clearing the active stage restores the ungraded background. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Clearing the active stage restores the ungraded background.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_24]
[flag tutorial_done_24]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_3]
